# {{.Name}}

An agent served over HTTP, made with [agentflow](https://github.com/omniaura/agentflow).
`assistant.af` declares the agent and its tools; `af gen` turns it into
`assistant_af.go`. Conversations live in Postgres, so any server can answer
any thread and a restart loses nothing.

## Run

```sh
go get github.com/omniaura/agentflow@latest github.com/omniaura/agentflow/adapters/afthreadpg@latest
go mod tidy
docker run -d --name {{.Name}}-pg -e POSTGRES_PASSWORD=pw -p 5432:5432 postgres:17-alpine
export DATABASE_URL=postgres://postgres:pw@localhost:5432/postgres?sslmode=disable
export ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=...          # or OPENAI_API_KEY and OPENAI_MODEL
export APP_TOKEN=$(openssl rand -hex 16)
go run .
```

It creates its tables on start (`afthreadpg.Migrate`).

## Talk to it

```sh
auth="Authorization: Bearer $APP_TOKEN"
# Start a thread.
thread=$(curl -s -H "$auth" -d '{"agent":"assistant"}' localhost:8080/threads | jq -r .id)
# Send a message and stream the answer.
curl -N -H "$auth" -H 'Accept: text/event-stream' -d '{"message":"What time is it in Tokyo?"}' localhost:8080/threads/$thread/messages
# Or send it, and read the conversation once it's answered.
curl -s -H "$auth" -d '{"message":"And in Paris?"}' localhost:8080/threads/$thread/messages
curl -s -H "$auth" localhost:8080/threads/$thread/messages
```

`GET /threads/{thread}/runs` lists the agent's runs, and
`GET /threads/{thread}/runs/{run}/events` follows one, resumable with
`Last-Event-ID`.

## Change it

- **The agent**: edit `assistant.af`, then run `go tool af gen prompts .` (or `af gen prompts .`).
- **Tools**: add a `.tool` to `assistant.af`; `af gen` adds a method to
  `AssistantTools`, which you write in `tools.go`.
- **Users**: `owner` in `main.go` lets in one user holding `APP_TOKEN`.
  Replace it with your authentication; each user's threads are their own.
